lause: \"work-item tags widen one need without merging siblings;\"\n\nProposed `method`, whole cell:\n\nExercise each state of the hat block: a non-round neither reads the roster nor asks a perspective question; a first-approved system requirement or amended approved need makes the round, and every judged system requirement's need and every amended need is a parent; work-item tags widen one need without merging siblings; the authoring work item's tags widen them on both routes: a minted row's authoring cell supplies its tags in place of its own, the minted and in-lane rows for one system requirement compose one hat set, and a row whose cell is empty widens by its own tags; an absent roster supplies the no-perspective line; an unreadable roster refuses and names it; each applicable perspective receives one non-ruling outcome line; declared template slots receive the block while undeclared slots compose unchanged; a combined sitting carries one union block; and those outcome lines do not alter parsed row rulings or judged rows.\n\n## TC-399 `expected` (P7)\n\nProposed `expected`, whole cell:\n\nSatisfies LLR-360 (parent SR-161): a decomposition-round sitting presents each applicable perspective question and requires one outcome, while another sitting has no perspective question; the two routes put one hat set for one system requirement; optional-slot, combined-sitting, absent-roster, unreadable-roster, and verdict-parsing outcomes remain as stated.\n\nThe tests as built match this text: `test_a_real_mint_and_the_lane_row_compose_one_hat_set` (one hat set), `test_a_non_empty_authoring_cell_supplies_the_tags_in_place_of_the_row_cells` and `test_the_authoring_cell_widens_each_need_and_sibling_needs_never_merge` (in place of its own), and `test_an_empty_authoring_cell_reads_the_two_row_cells` with `test_a_range_sweep_with_no_merged_leaves_the_cell_empty_and_widens_by_its_own_tags` (empty cell). No test was renamed or added in this stage, so TC-399's `evidence` stands.\n\n## Cells checked and found right\n\n- LLR-360 `module` already names `hats.py` and `intake.py`. Its `code_symbol` already names `context_from_work_item` and `_authoring_tags`, and both symbols now exist. Nothing to change.\n- IF-092 `data` matches the shipped contract body. It stays `v1`.\n- LLR-360 `detail` and SR-161 need no text.\n\n## Other rows\n\nNothing else. No row's traced cell is now wrong. `docs/interface-reference.md` line 869 still reads \"19-column\": it is generated from the contract body, so the coordinator's landing regeneration carries it.\n\r\n--- SETTLED DIFF ---\r\ndiff --git a/docs/decisions/wi-982.toml b/docs/decisions/wi-982.toml\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..cdac0aa14\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/decisions/wi-982.toml\n@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@\n+# docs/decisions/wi-982.toml — delegated calls in WI-982's lane.\n+# Format: project-trajectory/decisions.template.toml.\n+\n+high_risk = []\n+\n+[decision.D-001]\n+decided = \"REVIEW-B stands in as Claude Opus at high for each round of this lane (ruling 7; coordinator-2026-10-16 D-008), recorded here as the substitution each lane owes until WI-815's Gemini route has one verified launch.\"\n+alternative = \"None: the slot has no other route today.\"\n+reversal_cost = \"Low: a round re-runs.\"\n+why_not_escalated = \"A standing owner ruling.\"\n+review = \"\"\n+\n+[decision.D-002]\n+decided = \"The build ran as two fresh foreground builders, tests then code, in place of one resumed builder, since a resumed builder reports only in the background in a headless leg. Three differences from the plan are accepted as within its scope. tests/test_wi_loader_sync.py gained the new key in its six row fixtures, the same edit Adopted and Digests took, or the smoke tier errors with KeyError. intake.py grew 18 SLOC where the plan said about 13, stamped per row (1872 to 1890). The WI-000 row of the work-items template was already short of its header, and this row leaves that as it found it, the row being inert.\"\n+a